<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-repairability> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/bibliographicCitation> "EU DPP Textile Repairability Ontology. Version 1.1.2."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-repairability> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-07-01"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-repairability> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> "Elio Hbeich"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-repairability> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Ontology module for textile repairability-related product aspects, services, guidance, design features, contextual conditions, priority elements, assessments, repair-related process specialisations and their links to EU DPP product-event semantics. The module does not define a universal objective repairability score."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-repairability> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2026-07-01"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-repairability> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-repairability> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-07-16"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-repairability> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://susproc.jrc.ec.europa.eu/product-bureau/sites/default/files/2025-12/Textile-Prep-Study_3rd-Milestone_20251212.pdf> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-repairability> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "EU DPP Textile Repairability Ontology"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-repairability> <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespacePrefix> "txtrep" .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-repairability> <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespaceUri> "https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-repairability#" .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-repairability> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The JRC concludes that textile-apparel repairability cannot currently be represented by a simple objective framework. This ontology therefore represents evidence and enabling conditions without inferring that a product is objectively repairable."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-repairability> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The module reuses the semantic product-event classes defined in the EU DPP EVENT module. Textile-specific life-extension event classes bridge those event semantics with concrete textile process executions; EPCIS technical carriers remain defined by the EVENT module."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-repairability> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "EU DPP Textile Repairability Ontology"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-repairability> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "Version 1.1.2" .
